---
description: Захватить в хранилище исходной базы изменённые объекты ветки
agent: code
---

Use this command only from an active ready configuration `itldev/*` worktree whose source infobase uses a configuration repository.

Run the helper directly from the current project directory:

If the agent shell tool supports `timeout_ms`, run this lifecycle command with `timeout_ms >= 3900000` by default so the outer shell outlives the 3600-second 1C Designer/Enterprise limit. Do not use `120000 ms` or another short default.

```powershell
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\.agents\skills\1c-workflow\scripts\run-itl-command.ps1 -- -Action lock-config-repository-objects
```

The helper maps committed, staged, unstaged, deleted, and untracked configuration delta to an official XML object list and invokes only `/ConfigurationRepositoryLock -Objects` against the source infobase. It never loads configuration files and never widens the request to the full configuration. New top-level metadata identities require a separate root-only capture (`Configuration includeChildObjects="false"`) before the remaining objects. New forms or attributes inside an existing object do not trigger that dependency. A failed root operation prevents the second request; the report names dependent new objects and the observed owner. Root ownership alone never means that new objects were individually captured. An empty list is a successful no-op; unresolved paths or ambiguous metadata identity block before Designer starts. Return a non-empty `userReport` exactly, including when `status=failed`: it preserves successful captures, conflicting owners, absent objects and unconfirmed outcomes. Apply the same `userReportOmitted` file recovery on failure as on success. Preserve the failed status and append its `requiredAction`; do not replace a partial report with only the first conflict or automatically retry/unlock objects. If no report exists and `LOCK_CONFIG_REPOSITORY_OBJECT_CONFLICT` already names the exact objects and repository users, report that error and its `requiredAction` directly without reading `console.log`. For other failures without a report, read only the last 80 lines of `logPath`.

The shared database queue reserves the source infobase before local lifecycle locks and retains ownership through both requests and confirmed cleanup. Existing owners finish normally; do not close foreign sessions to bypass the wait. Branch and Vanessa service databases are not part of this command's reservation.
